# A tag's pattern names a field once, as a record's does (neg pattern-field-twice on the
# claude-bugs branch: "`x` is matched twice") and as an element applied does ("`label` is
# given twice"): a second pattern for one field is refused. The checker lets it through
# today. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

Name: fn Element Ui.* o -> Text
fn Name e = match e:
    Ui.Button($label=$a, $label=$b): "button"
    otherwise: "other"

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Name (Ui.Label($text=$"x"))}")
